WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:09.580
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and it was just
announced that a live action Teen Titans series

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:14.350
is close to landing on TNT.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.420
In the tradition of Arrow it would just be
called Titans.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.610
But it’s not being done by the same group
of people that are doing Arrow and The Flash.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.510
So this video will be a breakdown of what’s
going on with the deal and which characters

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:23.610
they’ve confirmed for it.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.260
It’s still a very preliminary thing.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.610
If you are just finding me for the first time.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.789
There are 4 new DC Comics tv shows coming
in the next month.

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:32.970
Including Arrow, The Flash, Gotham and Constantine.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.430
I’ll be doing weekly videos for all of them,
so be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:43.019
Some of you guys have been asking me Teen
Titans questions on Twitter and Facebook.

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:48.820
The biggest being who’s on the team and
will it connect with the other DC shows?

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.730
Right now they’ve only named 3 team members,
Nightwing, Starfire and Raven.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.590
In the same way that Arrow and The Flash have
been casting superheroes using their real

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.920
names, the Teen Titans show lists Nightwing
as Dick Grayson.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.960
I know it sounds weird, but when they cast
these types of shows.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.260
They list Dick Grayson on the casting sheet,
not Nightwing.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.190
Right now there are no official plans to connect
it to the DC TV Universe in the way Arrow,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:23.710
The Flash, Constantine and Gotham will loosely
be connected.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.930
And to be honest, only Arrow and The Flash
have confirmed they’re doing full blown

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.330
crossovers.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:35.360
I’ll explain the shared TV Universe in a
sec.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.340
But the Teen Titans show would be a one hour
drama just like the other shows.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.700
Every live action DC Show right now is a one
hour drama.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.840
The current state of the production deal is
still at the pilot stage.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.550
Meaning, TNT is still waiting to approve the
pilot for production.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:50.550
If they say yes.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.430
TNT would pay 4 or 5 Million dollars for Warner
Brothers to produce a pilot episode.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.450
Then TNT would either greenlight the series
for 6 or so episodes.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.150
And if those go well, they’d pick it up
for a full season.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:05.909
And each season thereafter they’d either
pick it up and cancel.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:15.780
That’s typically the way all tv shows work.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:29.730
The only exception to that right now inside
the DC Universe is Gotham.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:35.030
Fox paid Warner Brothers a dump truck of money
to produce the show themselves and greenlit

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.730
a full season 1 almost immediately.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:42.670
Usually shows don’t get a full season order
that fast unless they’re a guaranteed hit.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:47.180
TNT doesn’t have FOX levels of money to
throw around, but they do need a Superhero

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.180
Genre show.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.400
So TNT really wants Teen Titans to work.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.680
If you want to know what it might look like.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:59.520
Think about the other shows TNT is running
and how a new superhero drama might fit in

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.520
with those.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.370
Right now they’ve got the new Sean Bean
show Legends, Major Crimes, Murder In The

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:11.620
First, Perception, Cold Justice, and reruns
of Supernatural, Smallville and some other

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.260
younger demographic shows.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:18.270
Basically right now, TNT is like the Informative
Murder Porn channel for those who saw that

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.270
episode of South Park.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.959
If you didn’t you should watch it, it’s
on Hulu.

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:24.250
So any Superhero show they’d want to do
would combine some of the feel of their syndicated

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.700
shows so people like me would watch with the
gritty hardcore aspects of Informative Murder

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.700
Porn.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:36.400
So the older TNT audience, like people 25
to 54 years old.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:47.510
Mostly skewing towards the older half of that
range.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.379
So imagine a bloodier more sexed up disturbing
version of Arrow.

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:52.780
And that’s really what would probably sell
at TNT.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.640
They’re going to want a show that fits in
with their other new shows.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.640
So just remember that.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.069
I think it’s an interesting twist.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:02.190
TNT is a cable network, so it doesn’t have
to worry as much about censorship issues as

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.629
say Gotham on FOX.

00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:09.940
Gotham is supposed to be really dark and gritty,
but it’s on a major network.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.959
So it can only take that so far.

00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:15.420
Cable shows have a lot more lattitude in what
they can show.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:21.680
And since this isn’t an animated show being
marketed to children there’s also not those

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.680
concerns.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.650
The other big question that I’ve seen a
few of you ask is who is behind this, like

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:29.550
who’s the person writing all this stuff.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:32.360
It’s Akiva Goldsman and Marc Haimes.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.990
Most people will remember Goldsman as the
person who wrote Batman Forever and Batman

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.430
and Robin, that is not a strike in his favor.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.819
But he also wrote on Fringe for a long time.

00:04:41.819 --> 00:04:44.669
Haimes isn’t really known for his writing.

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:47.699
He used to be an executive at Dreamworks,
I don’t know that he still is.

00:04:47.699 --> 00:04:52.870
Right now the story of that Pilot episode
is essentially set.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.810
TNT is just finalizing the deal.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:01.630
So this is happening but it doesn’t guarantee
it will make it to series.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.699
If you remember, during the Smallville era,
Warner Brothers tried to get a Blue Beetle

00:05:04.699 --> 00:05:05.699
show off the ground.

00:05:05.699 --> 00:05:09.419
They even shot a pilot episode, Geoff Johns
brought footage to Comic Con.

00:05:09.419 --> 00:05:10.919
But it never turned into a series.

00:05:10.919 --> 00:05:16.259
So there have been big DC TV Shows that fizzled
out in various stages of development.

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:24.139
In terms of what the story might be, based
on them only announcing three members it’s

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:35.300
probably going to be an origin story with
twenty something-aged characters.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:38.000
So this won’t be like a high school version
of Teen Titans, it won’t be Buffy.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:43.789
Arrow took it’s time introducing other characters
from the comics, The Flash is getting there

00:05:43.789 --> 00:06:04.029
a lot faster, but since those are both CW
shows and they share a lot of the same DNA,

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:08.339
I don’t expect TNT to just jump right in
with every Teen Titan team member there’s

00:06:08.339 --> 00:06:09.339
ever been.

00:06:09.339 --> 00:06:14.710
In terms of big season 1 villains they might
use, some of my top picks would be Trigon,

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.550
if they’re doing Raven, they can do Trigon.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:21.960
HIVE, Vandal Savage, Cheshire, Calculator.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:26.879
I don’t think Warner Brothers would let
them use Deathstroke, since Arrow already

00:06:26.879 --> 00:06:27.879
did the character.

00:06:27.879 --> 00:06:36.399
Warner Brothers and DC have to approve when
shows want to use characters for the first

00:06:36.399 --> 00:06:37.399
time.

00:06:37.399 --> 00:06:40.990
For example, during the Arrow Comic Con panel,
Andrew Kreisberg said that initially when

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:45.349
they were planning season 3, they wanted to
use Ted Kord as the Blue Beetle.

00:06:45.349 --> 00:06:49.380
They’d already laid all these Kord Industries
easter eggs everywhere, so it’s only natural

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.710
they’d bring him on.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.309
But, Warner Brothers said “We have other
plans for that character.”

00:06:54.309 --> 00:06:58.129
- So naturally, they made Brandon Routh’s
Character the Ray Palmer Atom.

00:06:58.129 --> 00:07:03.439
Re-thinking Kriesberg’s comment about Blue
Beetle makes me wonder if Ted Kord is in this

00:07:03.439 --> 00:07:04.479
new Titan’s show.

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:10.819
It’s not confirmation or anything, but Warners
did have other plans for a live action Ted

00:07:10.819 --> 00:07:11.819
Kord.

00:07:11.819 --> 00:07:14.809
And it’s probably not for Batman vs Superman.

00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:19.499
Of course if everything works out I’d love
to see Tim Drake, Cyborg, Beast Boy, Wondergirl

00:07:19.499 --> 00:07:20.499
and maybe even Superboy.

00:07:20.499 --> 00:07:25.120
I think the long shots are Superboy and Wondergirl,
just because the Superman/Wonder Woman persona’s

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.490
have typically been film-only.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:31.409
But it’s possible we could see a live action
Conner Kent someday.

00:07:31.409 --> 00:07:32.409
Probably not soon.

00:07:32.409 --> 00:07:36.869
Because you’d have to explain superman in
the new tv universe first, lex luthor again

00:07:36.869 --> 00:07:39.409
and it just makes things so much more complicated.

00:07:39.409 --> 00:07:44.619
I know you guys all say Smallville did it
before, but think of the new DC TV Universe

00:07:44.619 --> 00:07:46.529
as beginning with Arrow.

00:07:46.529 --> 00:07:49.439
Arrow is the progenitor for all these new
Modern Shows.

00:07:49.439 --> 00:07:55.330
So everything has to be re-introduced just
like in the comics after the new 52 universe.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:08:00.360
Just pretend like Smallville isn’t canon
with all these new stories.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:08.639
Given that, let me know who you guys want
to see be the villain of the Teen Titans show?

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:15.509
Remember, it can’t be someone that’s already
been on another show in the last couple of

00:08:15.509 --> 00:08:16.509
years.

00:08:16.509 --> 00:08:22.189
TNT is a different network than CW and while
all these different networks are doing shows.

00:08:22.189 --> 00:08:26.589
Each network isn’t doing characters the
other networks are doing.

00:08:26.589 --> 00:08:29.879
Since we’re within 4 weeks of all these
shows premiering, Next week I’m going to

00:08:29.879 --> 00:08:34.110
start doing bonus videos for them, especially
the new stuff like Gotham, Constantine and

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.110
The Flash.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.110
I already do a lot of Arrow videos.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.110
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:42.479
And if there’s any video requests you guys
want to make, just let me know in the comments.

00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:47.590
Right now click here to learn all about the
new Arrow Season 3 trailer and click here

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.450
to learn about some of the new Flash Villains
coming in season 1.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.620
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

